the team has access to the information and
resources they need to do their best work.

50
00:03:18,720 --> 00:03:22,823
You do this through regular communication,
accessible documentation, and

51
00:03:22,823 --> 00:03:26,677
regular check-ins with the team to listen,
share information, ask and

52
00:03:26,677 --> 00:03:29,630
answer questions and provide support.

53
00:03:29,630 --> 00:03:30,818
As a project manager,

54
00:03:30,818 --> 00:03:34,509
you're in the perfect spot to identify
work that might be a good fit for

55
00:03:34,509 --> 00:03:38,720
a person who really wants it, but
who shies away from asking for it.

56
00:03:38,720 --> 00:03:43,070
Knowing an individual's aspirations will
help you highlight these opportunities.

57
00:03:43,070 --> 00:03:46,488
Finally, to invite and
integrate diverse perspectives,

58
00:03:46,488 --> 00:03:51,272
it's your role to cultivate a culture in
which each team member's perspective can

59
00:03:51,272 --> 00:03:56,040
be openly shared, heard and
integrated into work related decisions.

60
00:03:56,040 --> 00:03:59,579
You do this by creating a sense of
psychological safety on the team and

61
00:03:59,579 --> 00:04:03,178
by inviting teammates to share
their thoughts, ideas and concerns,

62
00:04:03,178 --> 00:04:05,510
regardless of their role or
rank on the team.

63
00:04:07,590 --> 00:04:08,946
Developing ethical and

64
00:04:08,946 --> 00:04:12,670
inclusive leadership skills
